<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Case study on handling a Composition-type question using ToG, PPDR with chain reasoning (denoted as PPDR(C) in the table), and PPDR with parallel reasoning (denoted as PPDR(P)). <span id="A1.T8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Underline</span> text indicates incorrect parts.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2.SSSx4.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conjunction type question</h5>

<div id="A1.SSx2.SSSx4.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.SSSx4.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Table <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Conjunction type question ‣ Case Study on Composition and Conjunction type question ‣ Result Detail ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Beyond Chains: Bridging Large Language Models and Knowledge Bases in Complex Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we observe that PPDR(P) retrieves triples that strictly follow the reasoning logic and successfully leads to the correct answer. In contrast, PPDR with chain reasoning falls into logical confusion and fails to produce the correct answer, even after multiple reasoning steps. Similarly, ToG also fails to follow the parallel reasoning logic and cannot arrive at the correct answer.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T9" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T9.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T9.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:1pt 4.6pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A1.T9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_leader"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:0.8pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r" style="padding:1pt 4.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T9.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T9.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T9.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:1pt 4.6pt;" colspan="2">What is there to see in Mountain Time Zone near the Grand Canyon?</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:1pt 4.6pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A1.T9.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_leader"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:0.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
